From 7836047a80dc46f68d409bf0429af56b1740a3b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gianni <rel037@localhost>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 23:37:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] launcher 2.6.2: every update failure shows its reason and
 is logged; missing files repair themselves

Settings > Updates, the status rail and its tip now say what went wrong instead of "Update check failed", and a failed action the player started is explained once in a message. Every step goes to updates\launcher-update.log (host, HTTP status, WinHTTP and Windows errors, the file involved), rotated at 256 KB.

Leftover staging and package.zip(.part) are cleared on every start and before every attempt; a folder Windows will not remove is named. Each downloaded file gets three tries, and a file the antivirus blocks or removes after writing (access denied, error 225/226) names the file and asks for a folder exception. That reason survives the fall-back to the full package.

A current install with missing or wrong-size files (for example a quarantined engine) is repaired on start, and an install without its engine fetches a newer version right away. Verify and repair now works from any state, including a missing engine. It re-hashes every staged file after the copy and reports "Repaired N files". An interrupted copy is detected on the next start. The launcher's own update is still offered when the game update fails, and after a failed apply.

New headless checks: --update-test --repair and --update-test --startup-check.
